S168, 2026-09-01. The reverse-futility floor re-taken over the 82.

  python3 adocs/data/S154_floor_margin_sweep.py floor
  python3 adocs/data/S154_floor_margin_sweep.py red

The floor was 8 over S145's 48, where the ends were 9 shipping and 7 with
the guard removed. Over the 82 the ends are 12 and 10, so the floor is 11.
DEC-116 is why it is re-derived rather than re-read: it is the second
re-derivation and both were forced by an end moving.

RfpMinPly swept at HEAD, RfpMaxDepth held at its shipping value.
The declared minimum is relaxed to 0 in a throwaway worktree: S142 made it 2,
so a shipping binary refuses 1 and 0 and answers with its default instead.
