=== The mates in three, split by motif ===

Computed from the masks above against adocs/data/S145_mate_set.tsv in file
order. 24 mates in three: 16 queen, 8 rook. Both knight rows are mates in two.

  motif   n    shipping   RfpMinPly 1   RfpMinPly 5
  queen   16      9            7             14
  rook     8      3            3              7

Two things follow. The queen rows reproduce S154's 9 / 7 / 14 exactly, so 34
added positions moved none of the old verdicts -- the same inertness S154
measured across seventeen commits and nine table sizes, seen here across a set
change. And the rook rows add a constant 3 to both ends rather than widening
the gap, so the floor moves from 8 to 11 while what it tolerates stays one loss.
